    "m_ObjectId": "1a2482ae7c384953a3151c31566e3243",
    "m_Title": "Performance Optimization: Distance Fields",
    "m_Content": "Implemented a bidirectional distance field, fed in as an input. Computer shader recomputes this value when geometry changes (same time as faces). 4 values per pixel, one for each entering direction. Each distance # is of voxels steps in that direction until any non-empty block encountered (regardless of how far you go in other directions).\n\nOptimization yields performance improvement, but only noticable when viewing along a single axis. Since this is the vast minority of cases, not worth the overhead of the additional instructions as well as the added complexity. Removed and went with simpler naive method that has less code.",
